HomaStack licence: NOT YET SELECTED
====================================

No open-source licence has been chosen for the HomaStack repository yet.
Until the project owners select one, the code in this repository is
"all rights reserved" by its authors by default. This file is a placeholder
so that the decision is visible and tracked; it is not itself a licence.

Decision needed
---------------
Pick a licence (common choices for Rust/.NET infrastructure are MIT,
Apache-2.0, or "MIT OR Apache-2.0"), replace this file with its text, and set
the `license` field in `rust/Cargo.toml` `[workspace.package]`.

Upstream licence obligations that constrain the choice
------------------------------------------------------
1. PlatformLab/HomaModule (Linux kernel module)
   https://github.com/PlatformLab/HomaModule
   Pinned revision: 4bd0275714439da2955670a6c438f6c23304d785 (2026-10-27)
   - `homa.h` (user-space API header):
       SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause OR GPL-2.0+ WITH Linux-syscall-note
     A verbatim copy is vendored at `rust/crates/homa-sys/upstream/homa.h`
     together with its man pages (`homa.7`, `sendmsg.2`, `recvmsg.2`), under
     the BSD-2-Clause option. The BSD-2-Clause notice is reproduced in
     `rust/crates/homa-sys/upstream/LICENSE-BSD-2-Clause`.
   - Kernel sources (`homa_*.c`, `homa_receiver.cc`): BSD-2-Clause OR GPL-2.0+.
     No implementation code was copied from them; they were read to verify
     the socket interface. The Rust code here is an independent
     implementation of the user-space side of that interface.
2. PlatformLab/Homa (older user-space C++ transport)
   https://github.com/PlatformLab/Homa
   Pinned revision: 6f0873de6b1b8cd060c21735c04de1fb9a27c693 (2022-11-09)
   Licence: ISC (Copyright (c) 2018-2019, Stanford University).
   Consulted for architecture only; no code copied.

Because only the BSD-2-Clause option of the vendored header is exercised,
any OSI-approved permissive licence (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD) is compatible.
